e work, bound every workload at or below 196608 elements: run() re-read ~20 pieces of tensor metadata (data_ptr, numel, element_size, shape comparisons, contiguity flags, device index, dict key with device.index) on every invocation, costing ~14us on top of a 10-16us raw launch. Memoizing the resolved flat dispatch behind three pointer comparisons plus numel and dtype brings those workloads to 13.4-14.3us. The same edit exposed a one-sided mask defect (backward streams bounded only below) which is also fixed.", "round_num": 4, "strategy_evolution": "Device work is essentially done for 6 of 9 timing cases; the remaining gains are confined to the three 1M-vector cases where the kernel is still 12-22x faster than the reference but above its own copy floor.", "debug_lesson_extra": ""}}
